---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site.config";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
---

<Base title={`About | ${site.name}`}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "About" }]} />
  <h1 class="mt-1 font-display text-[44px] leading-none font-bold text-balance">Good training, no coach.</h1>
  <p class="mt-4">
    Open Training gives you ready-made practice for the court. Pick a goal, and you get a 30-minute session of three
    drills that build on each other. Or pick a single shot, and you get drills that repeat only that shot, from calm to
    full pace. Every drill comes with a short video that shows how it is played.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold text-balance">Where the drills come from</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">The drills and tactics come from more than 200 reviewed YouTube videos by coaches and pros. Each drill plays the part of the video that shows it.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold text-balance">What's inside</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">
    Everything the sessions are built from, on one page: the shots and when in a point they come up, the combinations
    that link them, and the drills that are games. It is written for players and coaches who want to look under the hood.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-2"><a href="/overview/" data-overview-link class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center font-head font-bold underline underline-offset-4">See the Training System Overview →</a></p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold text-balance">How a session is built</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">
    The sessions follow sports-science research on how people learn movement skills. Each session is a ladder: Drill 1
    lets you find the shot, Drill 2 adds pressure, and Drill 3 puts it into a real point. Every step uses constraints,
    simple rules like a target zone, a limited number of shots or a point scored differently. Under such a rule, the right
    shot is the one that wins, so you learn it without anyone explaining it. Aim for about seven good balls in ten. If a
    drill is too easy or too hard, it tells you how to adjust it. AI helped turn the videos into drills and sessions,
    and I decide which ones go online.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold text-balance">Non-commercial</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">
    Open Training is a private, non-commercial project by Volker Max Meyer, a pickleball player in Berlin. No club or
    company runs it. There are no ads and no sign-up, and nothing is for sale. I want to help players get better and
    bring pickleball to the people.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold text-balance">Feedback welcome</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">
    Open Training is a work in progress. I add and change sessions and drills based on what players tell me. After a goal
    session, the short form at the end is the quickest way. For a shot drill, a missing drill or anything else, just email
    me at {site.contactEmail}.
  </p>
</Base>
